Elder: The merchant shared the baskets, and the farmer saved the fields. Dakal a salamat.
Elder: Now the village well needs help. Before we draw from it again, we use our old counting stones.
You: You will teach us the next numbers there?
Elder: Awa. I will teach you pitu, walo, siyam, and apulu.
Elder: Stand by the well. I will show the stones from above so you can see them light one by one.
Elder: Press E to continue, R to review, and F when you're ready to leave the lesson.
[end_timeline]
